# {{title}} Reference

Supporting detail for the `{{name}}` skill: the material an agent needs only
after deciding to do the work, kept out of the skill body so the body stays
short enough to read on load.

## What belongs here

Long tables, per-harness tool mappings, worked examples, API field lists,
anything that would push the skill body past a screen or two. The body should
stay a procedure; this file is the appendix it points at.

## What does not

Anything the agent needs in order to decide whether the skill applies at all.
That belongs in the body, or in the frontmatter trigger — a reference file is
read after the decision, so nothing that informs the decision can live here.

Replace this file's contents entirely. It exists so a new skill starts in the
multi-file shape rather than being retrofitted into it later, which is where
harness delivery differences show up.
